WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.040
Welcome to the CIS Controls v8 application security course.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.380
This course uses the OWASP Top 10 as a practical way to discuss common application risks

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.040
and connect them to defensive safeguards from the CIS Controls.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.180
Application security matters because modern applications handle identities,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.000
business workflows, integrations, and sensitive data.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.220
Weaknesses in software can increase attack surface, make monitoring harder,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.760
and create gaps in access control, vulnerability management, logging,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.740
and secure configuration.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.840
The CIS Controls provide a prioritized set of safeguards for practical cyber defense.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.180
Implementation Groups IG1, IG2,

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.040
and IG3 help organizations phase those safeguards based on risk, resources,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.020
and operational maturity.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.600
Throughout the course,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.780
each OWASP risk is mapped to selected CIS Controls or safeguards that commonly support

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:54.960
prevention,

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.340
detection, or remediation.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.080
These mappings are awareness aids, not audit conclusions,

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.780
and should be validated against your organization's environment and security program.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.480
As you move through the modules, focus on how secure development, least privilege,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.180
hardening, vulnerability management, monitoring, and response work together.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.880
The goal is to make application security part of repeatable defensive operations,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.780
not a one-time checklist.
